{"task_id": "Mbpp/89", "solution": "import math\n\ndef closest_num(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest integer strictly less than n.\n    Handles both integer and floating-point numeric inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(n, int):\n        return n - 1\n\n    # For floats, determine if it's effectively an integer-valued float.\n    # The design context defines FLOAT_EPS as 1e-12 for this check.\n    FLOAT_EPS = 1e-12\n\n    if math.fabs(n - round(n)) < FLOAT_EPS:\n        # If n is an integer-valued float (e.g., 11.0, 5.999...999), return int(n) - 1.\n        return int(round(n)) - 1\n    else:\n        # For truly non-integer floats (e.g., 11.5), the largest integer strictly less than n is floor(n).\n        return int(math.floor(n))"}
