{"task_id": "Mbpp/87", "solution": "def merge_dictionaries_three(d1: dict, d2: dict, d3: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merges three dictionaries into a single dictionary, with later dictionaries overriding earlier ones on key conflicts.\n    All keys and values are converted to strings in the resulting dictionary.\n    \"\"\"\n    result: dict[str, str] = {}\n\n    d1_normalized = {str(k): str(v) for k, v in d1.items()}\n    d2_normalized = {str(k): str(v) for k, v in d2.items()}\n    d3_normalized = {str(k): str(v) for k, v in d3.items()}\n\n    result.update(d1_normalized)\n    result.update(d2_normalized)\n    result.update(d3_normalized)\n\n    return result"}
