{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) using dynamic programming.\n    Handles base cases A(0,0)=1 and A(n,m)=0 if m < 0 or m >= n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize dp array for A(1,j). A(1,0)=1.\n    # dp[j] stores A(k, j) for the current k.\n    # The length of dp for A(k,j) is k.\n    dp = [1]  # Represents A(1,0)\n\n    # Iterate from k = 2 up to n\n    for k in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Create new_dp for A(k,j). It will have k elements (j from 0 to k-1).\n        new_dp = [0] * k\n        for j in range(k):\n            # Recurrence: A(k,j) = (k - j) * A(k-1, j-1) + (j + 1) * A(k-1, j)\n            term1 = (k - j) * (dp[j - 1] if j - 1 >= 0 else 0)\n            term2 = (j + 1) * (dp[j] if j < len(dp) else 0)\n            new_dp[j] = term1 + term2\n        dp = new_dp\n\n    return dp[m]"}
