{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is the majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Binary search to find the first occurrence of x\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    first_occurrence_idx = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            first_occurrence_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # If x is not found, it cannot be a majority element\n    if first_occurrence_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Check the element at first_occurrence_idx + n // 2\n    # If it's still x, then x occurs more than n/2 times\n    majority_check_index = first_occurrence_idx + n // 2\n    \n    return majority_check_index < n and arr[majority_check_index] == x"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of a non-negative integer.\n    For negative integers, it counts set bits of their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    num = abs(n)  # Use absolute value to handle negative numbers and ensure termination.\n    while num > 0:\n        num &= (num - 1)  # Clear the least significant set bit.\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "def next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    Returns 1 for n values of 0 or 1, otherwise calculates using bitwise operations.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n    # For positive n > 1, find the number of bits needed for (n-1), then left-shift 1 by that amount.\n    # This effectively finds the next power of 2.\n    return 1 << (n - 1).bit_length()"}
