{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(items: list[tuple], *, strict: bool = False) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of tuples in a list, treating tuples with identical elements\n    in different order as the same by normalizing them to a sorted form.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrence_counts = {}\n    for item_tuple in items:\n        # Normalize the tuple by sorting its elements to create a canonical key.\n        canonical_key = tuple(sorted(item_tuple))\n        occurrence_counts[canonical_key] = occurrence_counts.get(canonical_key, 0) + 1\n    return occurrence_counts"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-positioned bits (0-based odd indices) in the given number.\n    This interpretation ensures the example `even_bit_set_number(10) == 10` holds.\"\"\"\n\n    # Determine the required bit-width for the number n.\n    # For n=0, n.bit_length() is 0, so max(1, 0) = 1 ensures a minimal width for mask generation.\n    width = max(1, n.bit_length())\n\n    # Generate a mask with bits set at odd 0-based positions (1, 3, 5, ...).\n    mask = 0\n    for pos in range(width):\n        if pos % 2 == 1:\n            mask |= (1 << pos)\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set the identified \"even bits\" in n.\n    return n | mask"}
