{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts sequences of length n, where each element is a positive integer,\n    greater than or equal to twice the previous, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_min_val: int, length_remaining: int) -> int:\n        key = (current_min_val, length_remaining)\n        if key in memo:\n            return memo[key]\n\n        # Base case 1: If no length remaining, a valid sequence segment has been formed.\n        if length_remaining == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        # Base case 2: If the minimum possible value for the current element\n        # exceeds the global maximum 'm', no valid sequence can be formed starting here.\n        if current_min_val > m:\n            return 0\n\n        # Base case 3 (optimization): If only one element is remaining,\n        # any integer from current_min_val to m is a valid choice.\n        if length_remaining == 1:\n            result = max(0, m - current_min_val + 1)\n            memo[key] = result\n            return result\n\n        total_sequences = 0\n        # Iterate through possible values 'x' for the current element.\n        # 'x' must be at least 'current_min_val' and at most 'm'.\n        for x in range(current_min_val, m + 1):\n            next_min_for_subproblem = 2 * x\n\n            # Optimization: If the minimum value for the next element already exceeds 'm',\n            # then all subsequent 'x' choices in this loop will also lead to a next_min > m,\n            # resulting in 0 from sub-calls. We can break early.\n            if next_min_for_subproblem > m:\n                break\n\n            total_sequences += _count_sequences_recursive(next_min_for_subproblem, length_remaining - 1)\n\n        memo[key] = total_sequences\n        return total_sequences\n\n    # Initial call: The first element can be any positive integer, so its minimum value is 1.\n    # We are looking for a sequence of total length 'n'.\n    return _count_sequences_recursive(1, n)"}
