{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the left-most (most significant) unset bit in a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Get the number of bits required to represent n (position of MSB + 1)\n    b = n.bit_length()\n    \n    # Iterate from the MSB down to the LSB\n    for pos in range(b - 1, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the bit at the current position is unset\n        if not (n >> pos) & 1:\n            # If unset, set this bit and return the new value\n            return n | (1 << pos)\n            \n    # If all bits up to n.bit_length() are set, set the next higher bit\n    return n | (1 << b)"}
