{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(a: list[float], b: list[float], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size n.\n    The median is the average of the n-th and (n+1)-th smallest elements in the combined sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def find_kth_element(arr1: list[float], start1: int, end1: int,\n                         arr2: list[float], start2: int, end2: int, k: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively finds the k-th smallest element in the merged sorted arrays.\n        This uses a divide-and-conquer approach with O(log N) time and O(1) extra space.\n        \"\"\"\n        len1 = end1 - start1 + 1\n        len2 = end2 - start2 + 1\n\n        # Handle cases where one array is exhausted\n        if len1 == 0:\n            return float(arr2[start2 + k - 1])\n        if len2 == 0:\n            return float(arr1[start1 + k - 1])\n\n        # Base case for k=1 (the smallest element)\n        if k == 1:\n            return float(min(arr1[start1], arr2[start2]))\n\n        # Calculate the number of elements to consider from each array in the current step\n        num_to_take_from_arr1 = min(len1, k // 2)\n        num_to_take_from_arr2 = min(len2, k // 2)\n\n        # Get the \"mid\" values for comparison\n        # (start + num_to_take - 1) gives the actual index of the 'num_to_take'-th element\n        val1 = arr1[start1 + num_to_take_from_arr1 - 1]\n        val2 = arr2[start2 + num_to_take_from_arr2 - 1]\n\n        # Compare values to eliminate half of the elements from consideration\n        if val1 < val2:\n            # The k-th element cannot be among the first 'num_to_take_from_arr1' elements of arr1.\n            # Discard these elements and adjust k.\n            return find_kth_element(arr1, start1 + num_to_take_from_arr1, end1,\n                                    arr2, start2, end2, k - num_to_take_from_arr1)\n        else:\n            # The k-th element cannot be among the first 'num_to_take_from_arr2' elements of arr2.\n            # Discard these elements and adjust k.\n            return find_kth_element(arr1, start1, end1,\n                                    arr2, start2 + num_to_take_from_arr2, end2, k - num_to_take_from_arr2)\n\n    # The combined array has 2*n elements.\n    # The median is the average of the n-th and (n+1)-th smallest elements (1-indexed k).\n    \n    # Find the n-th smallest element\n    n_th_element = find_kth_element(a, 0, n - 1, b, 0, n - 1, n)\n    \n    # Find the (n+1)-th smallest element\n    n_plus_1_th_element = find_kth_element(a, 0, n - 1, b, 0, n - 1, n + 1)\n    \n    return (n_th_element + n_plus_1_th_element) / 2.0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/624", "solution": "from typing import Any, Optional\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input to the string conversion service.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass StringValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates if the input is a string.\"\"\"\n    allowed_types = (str,)\n\n    def validate(self, s: Any) -> bool:\n        if not isinstance(s, self.allowed_types):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a str\")\n        return True\n\nclass StringService:\n    \"\"\"Converts a string to uppercase and can optionally record history.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: StringValidator, repository: Optional[Any] = None):\n        self._validator = validator\n        self._repo = repository\n\n    def to_upper(self, s: str) -> str:\n        self._validator.validate(s)\n        out = s.upper()\n        # History recording is optional and not enabled for the default `is_upper` call.\n        return out\n\ndef is_upper(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts the given string to uppercase.\"\"\"\n    validator = StringValidator()\n    service = StringService(validator)\n    return service.to_upper(s)"}
