{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum average path from top-left to bottom-right in a square matrix.\n    Paths only allow right or down movements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n    \n    # dp[r][c] will store the maximum sum to reach cell (r, c).\n    dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Base case: starting cell (0,0)\n    dp[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row (only move right is possible)\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c-1] + float(matrix[0][c])\n\n    # Fill the first column (only move down is possible)\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r-1][0] + float(matrix[r][0])\n\n    # Fill the rest of the dp table\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            val = float(matrix[r][c])\n            # The maximum sum to reach (r,c) is its value plus the maximum sum from either the cell above or to its left.\n            dp[r][c] = max(dp[r-1][c], dp[r][c-1]) + val\n                \n    # The maximum total sum path ends at the bottom-right cell.\n    max_total_sum = dp[n-1][n-1]\n    \n    # All valid paths (right or down movements only) in an N x N matrix have a fixed length of 2N - 1 cells.\n    path_length = 2 * n - 1\n    \n    # Calculate the maximum average.\n    max_average = max_total_sum / path_length\n    \n    return max_average"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/722", "solution": "def filter_data(students: dict[str, tuple[float, float]], min_height: float, min_weight: float) -> dict[str, tuple[float, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Filters students whose height and weight meet or exceed the specified minimums.\"\"\"\n    filtered_students = {}\n    for name, (height, weight) in students.items():\n        if height >= min_height and weight >= min_weight:\n            filtered_students[name] = (height, weight)\n    return filtered_students"}
