{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "solution": "def sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of products of all possible contiguous sublists of a given list.\n    Uses an O(n) dynamic programming approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum_of_products = 0.0\n    # prev_end_sum stores the sum of products of all subarrays ending at the previous element.\n    # For a new element 'x', subarrays ending at 'x' are:\n    # 1. '[x]' (product is x)\n    # 2. '[..., x]' where '...' is a subarray ending at the previous element.\n    #    The sum of products for these is x * prev_end_sum.\n    # So, curr_end_sum = x + x * prev_end_sum = x * (1 + prev_end_sum).\n    prev_end_sum = 0.0\n\n    for x in nums:\n        curr_end_sum = x * (1.0 + prev_end_sum)\n        total_sum_of_products += curr_end_sum\n        prev_end_sum = curr_end_sum\n\n    return total_sum_of_products"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "def toggle_middle_bits(n: int) -> int:\n    # Determine the bit length (L) of the number.\n    # Special handling for n=0 to define its bit length as 1, as per design.\n    if n == 0:\n        L = 1\n    else:\n        L = n.bit_length()\n\n    # If the bit length is 2 or less, there are no \"middle\" bits to toggle.\n    # The number should be returned unchanged.\n    if L <= 2:\n        return n\n\n    # Calculate a mask that has '1's in the positions of the middle bits\n    # (from bit 1 to L-2) and '0's for the MSB (L-1) and LSB (0).\n    # First, create a sequence of (L-2) ones: (1 << (L - 2)) - 1.\n    # Then, shift these ones left by 1 position to start from bit 1.\n    mask = ((1 << (L - 2)) - 1) << 1\n\n    # Toggle the middle bits of 'n' by performing a bitwise XOR with the mask.\n    return n ^ mask"}
