{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "import math\n\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    This calculates the first k for which T_k (k*(k+1)/2) is greater than or equal to 10^(n-1).\n    \"\"\"\n    limit = 10 ** (n - 1)\n    # Solve k*(k+1)/2 >= limit for k: k^2 + k - 2*limit >= 0\n    # Using quadratic formula, k = (-1 + sqrt(1 + 8*limit)) / 2\n    discriminant = 1 + 8 * limit\n    sqrt_discriminant = math.isqrt(discriminant)\n    k = (sqrt_discriminant - 1) // 2\n    \n    # Check if the calculated k produces a triangular number that is too small.\n    # This can happen due to integer division truncating or if the exact square root wasn't enough.\n    if (k * (k + 1)) // 2 < limit:\n        k += 1\n    \n    return k"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(sorted_list, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the left insertion point for a value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    The index returned ensures that inserting the value at this position maintains sorted order.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] < value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
