{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(items, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by k positions.\n    Handles empty lists, positive, negative, and large k values.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(items)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Normalize k to be within [0, n-1]\n    # A negative k rotates to the left, which is equivalent to a right rotation by n - (abs(k) % n)\n    k_norm = k % n\n    \n    # Perform the rotation using slicing\n    return items[-k_norm:] + items[:-k_norm]"}
