{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "import re\n\ndef capital_words_spaces(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces between words in a string where a new word starts with a capital letter.\n    Handles camelCase, PascalCase, and acronyms like HTTPServer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Insert a space before an uppercase letter if it follows a lowercase letter or a digit.\n    result = re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z0-9])(?=[A-Z])', ' ', text)\n    # Insert a space if an uppercase letter is followed by another uppercase letter then a lowercase letter (acronym boundary).\n    result = re.sub(r'(?<=[A-Z])(?=[A-Z][a-z])', ' ', result)\n    return result"}
