{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index of the last occurrence, or -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    res = -1\n\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            res = mid\n            lo = mid + 1  # Try to find a larger index in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    return res"}
